 L117: ## Repository navigation\nL118: \nL119:   *   * cite62†Code L120:   * cite63†Issues249 (249) L121:   * cite64†Pull requests40 (40) L122:   * cite65†Actions L123:   * cite66†Projects L124:   * cite67†Security and quality L125:   * cite68†Insights L126: \nL127: More items\nL128: \nL129: ## Files Expand file tree\nL130: \nL131: main\nL132: \nL133: ## Breadcrumbs\nL134: \nL135:   1. cite69†DeepSeek-OCR L136: \nL137: /\nL138: \nL139: # README.md\nL140: \nL141: Copy path\nL142: \nL143: [Input: Go to file]\nL144: \nL145: Blame More file actions\nL146: \nL147: Blame More file actions\nL148: \nL149: ## Latest commit\nL150: \nL151: \nL152: \nL153: ## History\nL154: \nL155: History\nL156: \nL157: main\nL158: \nL159: ## Breadcrumbs\nL160: \nL161:   1. cite69†DeepSeek-OCR L162: \nL163: /\nL164: \nL165: # README.md\nL166: \nL167: Copy path\nL168: \nL169: Top\nL170: ## File metadata and controls\nL171: \nL172:   * Preview\nL173: \nL174:   * Code\nL175: \nL176:   * Blame\nL177: \nL178: 239 lines (197 loc) · 7.66 KB\nL179: \nL180: cite70†Raw L181: \nL182: Copy raw file\nL183: \nL184: Download raw file\nL185: \nL186: Outline\nL187: \nL188: Edit and raw actions\nL189: \nL190: * * *\nL191: \nL192: cite71†📥 Model Download†huggingface.co | cite72†📄 Paper Link | cite73†📄 Arxiv Paper Link†arxiv.org |\nL193: \nL194: ##\nL195: \nL196: cite74†DeepSeek-OCR: Contexts Optical Compression L197: \nL198: cite74†Explore the boundaries of visual-text compression. L199: ## Release\nL200: \nL201:   * [2026/01/27]🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀🚀 We present cite75†DeepSeek-OCR2 L202:   * [2025/10/23]🚀🚀🚀 DeepSeek-OCR is now officially supported in upstream cite76†vLLM†docs.vllm.ai . Thanks to the cite77†vLLM team for their help.\nL203:   * [2025/10/20]🚀🚀🚀 We release DeepSeek-OCR, a model to investigate the role of vision encoders from an LLM-centric viewpoint.\nL204: \nL205: ## Contents\nL206: \nL207:   * cite78†Install L208:   * cite79†vLLM Inference L209:   * cite80†Transformers Inference L210: ## Install\nL211: \nL212: > Our environment is cuda11.8+torch2.6.0.\nL213: \nL214:   1. Clone this repository and navigate to the DeepSeek-OCR folder\nL215: \nL216:     git clone https://github.com/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-OCR.git\nL217: \nL218:   2. Conda\nL219: \nL220:     conda create -n deepseek-ocr python=3.12.9 -y\nL221:     conda activate deepseek-ocr\nL222: \nL223:   3. Packages\nL224:   * download the vllm-0.8.5 cite81†whl L225: \nL226:     pip install torch==2.6.0 torchvision==0.21.0 torchaudio==2.6.0 --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu118\nL227:     pip install vllm-0.8.5+cu118-cp38-abi3-manylinux1_x86_64.whl\nL228:     pip install -r requirements.txt\nL229:     pip install flash-attn==2.7.3 --no-build-isolation\nL230: \nL231: Note: if you want vLLM and transformers codes to run in the same environment, you don't need to worry about this installation error like: vllm 0.8.5+cu118 requires transformers>=4.51.1\nL232: ## vLLM-Inference\nL233: \nL234:   * VLLM:\nL235: \nL236: > Note: change the INPUT_PATH/OUTPUT_PATH and other settings in the DeepSeek-OCR-master/DeepSeek-OCR-vllm/config.py\nL237: \nL238:     cd DeepSeek-OCR-master/DeepSeek-OCR-vllm\nL239: \nL240:   1. image: streaming output\nL241: \nL242:     python run_dpsk_ocr_image.py\nL243: \nL244:   2. pdf: concurrency ~2500tokens/s(an A100-40G)\nL245: \nL246:     python run_dpsk_ocr_pdf.py\nL247: \nL248:   3. batch eval for benchmarks\nL249: \nL250:     python run_dpsk_ocr_eval_batch.py\nL251: [2025/10/23] The version of upstream cite76†vLLM†docs.vllm.ai :\nL252: \nL253:     uv venv\nL254:     source .venv/bin/activate\nL255:     # Until v0.11.1 release, you need to install vLLM from nightly build\nL256:     uv pip install -U vllm --pre --extra-index-url https://wheels.vllm.ai/nightly\nL257: \nL258:     from vllm import LLM, SamplingParams\nL259:     from vllm.model_executor.models.deepseek_ocr import NGramPerReqLogitsProcessor\nL260:     from PIL import Image\nL261: \nL262:     # Create model instance\nL263:     llm = LLM(\nL264:         model=\"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-OCR\",\nL265:         enable_prefix_caching=False,\nL266:         mm_processor_cache_gb=0,\nL267:         logits_processors=[NGramPerReqLogitsProcessor]\nL268:     )\nL269: \nL270:     # Prepare batched input with your image file\nL271:     image_1 = Image.open(\"path/to/your/image_1.png\").convert(\"RGB\")\nL272:     image_2 = Image.open(\"path/to/your/image_2.png\").convert(\"RGB\")\nL273:     prompt = \"<image>\\n Free OCR.\"\nL274: \nL275:     model_input = [\nL276:         {\nL277:             \"prompt\": prompt,\nL278:             \"multi_modal_data\": {\"image\": image_1}\nL279:         },\nL280:         {\nL281:             \"prompt\": prompt,\nL282:             \"multi_modal_data\": {\"image\": image_2}\nL283:         }\nL284:     ]\nL285: \nL286:     sampling_param = SamplingParams(\nL287:                 temperature=0.0,\nL288:                 max_tokens=8192,\nL289:                 # ngram logit processor args\nL290:                 extra_args=dict(\nL291:                     ngram_size=30,\nL292:                     window_size=90,\nL293:                     whitelist_token_ids={128821, 128822},  # whitelist: <td>, </td>\nL294:                 ),\nL295:                 skip_special_tokens=False,\nL296:             )\nL297:     # Generate output\nL298:     model_outputs = llm.generate(model_input, sampling_param)\nL299: \nL300:     # Print output\nL301:     for output in model_outputs:\nL302:         print(output.outputs[0].text)\nL303: ## Transformers-Inference\nL304:   * Transformers\nL305: \nL306:     from transformers import AutoModel, AutoTokenizer\nL307:     import torch\nL308:     import os\nL309:     os.environ[\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES\"] = '0'\nL310:     model_name = 'deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-OCR'\nL311: \nL312:     tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name, trust_remote_code=True)\nL313:     model = AutoModel.from_pretrained(model_name, _attn_implementation='flash_attention_2', trust_remote_code=True, use_safetensors=True)\nL314:     model = model.eval().cuda().to(torch.bfloat16)\nL315:     # prompt = \"<image>\\nFree OCR. \"\n"
